answer_text:
When a credit licensee services an exempt SPFE, its IDR process should cover:
- the exempt SPFE’s activities;
- complaints that arise when the licensee acts as the representative of the exempt SPFE;
- complaints about the conduct of the exempt SPFE;
- complaints about both credit activities engaged in by the licensee under the servicing agreement and conduct of the exempt SPFE, including where changes are sought to the contract terms, for example on hardship grounds or because the contract was unsuitable or unjust.
